Key performance indicators
The Company uses a range of KPls to monitor financial performance. No specific benchmarks are set for
these KPI's, which are monitored as absolute measures and include the following:

The Company's income is driven mainly by the level of Assets Under Management (AUM) given that fee
income is based on the value of portfolios. Private Banking AUM managed on a Discretionary, Advisory or
Execution Only basis, excluding loans either directly or through a Financial Intermediary (FIM) grew by 10%
to £8.75bn (2022: £7.95bn).

Gross inflows into Discretionary or Advisory portfolios excluding internal transfers increased by £0.1bn to
£1.1 (2022: £1.0bn).

Regulatory measures
Common Equity Tier 1 ratio (CET1) increased to 22.3% from 20.3% and Liquidity Coverage Ratio (LCR)

increased to 274% compared to 218% in prior year.

