in 2023, we achieved a recycling rate of 65%, which means that we generated total of 29,700kgs of waste
out of which we were able to send 19,000kgs to recycling centres instead of landfills and the remaining
10,700kgs has been converted to generate 5,596kW energy and saving 25tonnes of CO2 and 179 trees.

Sustainability —- We know that sustainability is a key issue for clients and whilst we are already signatories to
the UN Principles for Responsible Investment (‘PRI’) and a member of the Climate Action 100+ Initiative, we
are, in conjunction with Quintet, continuing to enhance our investment approach integrating sustainability in
our thinking.

The Board of Directors played a key role in the definition of the corporate sustainability strategy (December
2023): between July and December 2023, the Board of Directors acted both as a stakeholder providing their
point of view on the materiality of sustainability for the bank, as well as validator of the final corporate
sustainability strategy. We are also committed to ensuring that our supply chain is free of any slavery and/or
human trafficking.

Further details regarding Sustainability can be found within the Task Force on Climate-related Financial
Disclosures (TCFD), which is set out on pages 18 to 26 of the Director's Report.

Risk Management
All key risks both financial and non-financial are disclosed in the Directors’ Report on pages 13 to 17.

Outlook

Geo-political uncertainty remains in the form of continuing events in Ukraine and tensions in the Middle East
which is impacting the global economy. Whilst the Company has reported a positive impact on interest margins
resulting from rising interest rates, investment fees have been challenged from the economic slowdown.
However, as we enter 2024, it is still unclear what shape any recovery will take. Despite these headwinds, the
Company remains well positioned to take advantage of its strategy, supporting clients, developing AUM and
lending opportunities as they arise.

This review has been prepared in line with guidance provided by the Financial Reporting Council to provide a
fair and balanced review of Brown Shipley’s business and prospects, without prejudicing the confidential
nature of commercially sensitive information.

