DIRECTORS’ REPORT

The Company also recognises that within the industry, it is normal practice for client facing managers to
receive a higher element of variable remuneration than managers in support functions and in some
circumstances such bonuses may be on a contractual basis.

A number of staff members are considered to be ‘Remuneration Code Staff or Material Risk Takers (‘MRTs’)
as defined in the Capital Requirements Regulation (‘CRR’). As at 31 December 2023, the Company has 18
such staff comprising the 6 Executive Committee members, 8 other senior management staff within control
functions and 4 front office relationship managers.

The variable element of remuneration for MRTs consists of bonuses under a Quintet MRTs bonus scheme
linked to Company and personal objectives. Of the annual award in respect of a performance year, 60% of
the bonus vests immediately and 40% is deferred equally over the next 3 years (in all cases each vested
amount is 50% in cash and 50% in phantom equity shares in Quintet). Where an MRT is not on the firm's
Executive Committee a de minimis of £100,000 applies before deferral is triggered. The phantom equity
shares are aligned to the net asset value of Quintet and therefore serve as a proxy for group performance.
Variable compensation awards of less than the de-minimus limit is included within the standard variable
compensation scheme for all other employees.

