Going Concern

The Directors have a reasonable expectation that the Company has adequate resources to continue in
operational existence for the foreseeable future, being a 12 month period to 31 March 2025. They therefore
continue to adopt the going concern basis of accounting in preparing the annual financial statements.

The Company has a strong financial position with good levels of capital and liquidity and has maintained a-
strong level of underlying profitability in recent years, which has enabled it to continue to invest in the business.
The Board has, like last year, undertaken steps to confirm the Company's going concern status this year, as
described in Note 1(a).

The Company only holds high quality, short-dated securities in its Treasury portfolio and has no exposure to
US banks or to Credit Suisse. The Company continues to monitor its Treasury activities and exposure limits
to individual counterparties on a regular basis, its capital ratios and liquidity metrics are strong and have not
deteriorated. The Company has adequate resources, even under a stress scenario to continue in operational
existence for the foreseeable future.

Further narrative around going concern is given on page 40 in the Notes to the Financial Statements.
Re-appointment of auditors
Ernst & Young LLP have indicated their willingness and have been re-appointed as auditor during the year,
and appropriate arrangements have been put in place for them to be appointed as auditor in the absence of
an Annual General Meeting.
Approved by the Board of Directors and signed on behalf of the Board.

