We obtained an understanding of the legal and regulatory frameworks that are applicable to the
Company and determined that the most significant relate to: the reporting framework (IFRS); the
regulations and supervisory requirements of the Prudential Regulation Authority (PRA); the Financial
Conduct Authority (FCA); and the relevant tax compliance legislation in the United Kingdom.

We understood how Brown Shipley & Co. Limited is complying with those frameworks by making
enquiries of management and the Audit Committee to understand how the Company maintains and
communicates its policies and procedures relating to these areas and corroborated this by reviewing
supporting documentation. We assessed the entity level controls framework of the Company to
consider whether appropriate measures are in place around fraud prevention.

We assessed the susceptibility of the Company’s financial statements to material misstatement,
including how fraud might occur by considering the risk of management override and assessed
revenue recognition to be a fraud risk. We incorporated data analytics into our testing of manual
journals, including testing segregation of duties, and into our testing of revenue recognition. We tested
specific transactions back to source documentation or independent confirmations, ensuring
appropriate authorisation of the transactions. Please refer back to the key audit matter for further
details.

Based on this understanding we designed our audit procedures to identify non-compliance with such
laws and regulations. Our procedures involved a review of the reporting to the Directors with respect to
the application of the documented policies and procedures and review of the financial statements to
ensure compliance with the reporting requirements of the Company.

We reviewed the breaches and complaints registers to identify any indication of breaches of laws and
regulations or systemic conduct issues, respectively. We have also reviewed regulatory
correspondence with the FCA and PRA.

A further description of our responsibilities for the audit of the financial statements is located on the
Financial Reporting Council's website at https:/Avwww.frc.org. uk/auditorsresponsibilities. This description forms
