DB Pension redress provisions

In late 2019 the Financial Conduct Authority wrote to regulated firms who had given advice on transfers from
defined benefit pension schemes in recent years and asked them to review the advice that was given. As a
result, the Company initiated a detailed review of advice given by the firm itself and by NW Brown prior to its
acquisition by the firm. An initial provision was made for the specific costs of assessing and calculating redress
for the cases identified. Loss assessments have been carried out by an independent specialist firm on each
identified case and all but a few cases have now been settled. The Company considers the provision as at 31
December 2023 to represent a reasonable estimate of the remaining cost to provide redress on those two
remaining cases.

The release of the provision in 2023 is due to the increase in market interest rates which has reduced the
amount of redress due. This release to the profit and loss account is offset in part by the increase in deferred
acquisition consideration referred to in Note 25 and the reduction in other debtors for PI insurance recoveries
referred to in Note 18.

