The Company also quantifies its exposure to interest rate risk using scenario analysis to simulate yield curve
shifts. This process considers the impact of +/- interest rate changes on the Company's Net interest Income
(‘NII’) and the change in Net Present Value (‘NPV’) of its expected cash flows (economic value of equity or
EVE method). The analysis considers a +/- 200bps parallel shift in rates, together with a range of parallel and
non-parallel interest rate shocks, as per the EBA guidelines.

