37 Events after the balance sheet date

In 2023, the Company entered into a legally binding agreement to sell its non-core client book of Court of
Protection assets under management for an estimated consideration of £1.36m. The transfer of the book
commenced in 2023 and £567k of proceeds have been recognised in the year. The remaining clients
transferred in the first quarter of 2024 and the remaining consideration will be recognised in that year.

On 26th January 2024, Brown Shipley signed an agreement to sell a book of Affluent clients to an external
third party. At the time of signing the accounts the sale has not been communicated to clients and it is too
early to estimate the financial impact of the sale.

